## Context

`AGENTS.md` and [[1060]] describe the merge gate `make check-fast` + `make lint`
as about 40 s. The 0870 integration review measured `make check-fast` at 322 to
462 s on doudou (load 2 to 4, `-n 4`), on five runs between 2026-09-29 12:00Z
and 14:00Z; one run of 441 s had 2040 tests passed. No padme figure without load
exists. The gate ran some fifteen times during that one review, so its cost
multiplies across every PR and every parallel session.

One cause is already known and fixed: before PR #1570 a JETP accounts test built
the real ledger twice (about 340 s of worker time) inside `check-fast`; it is now
marked `slow`. The rest is unmeasured. [[0041]] (deferred, April) and [[0038]]
cover pipeline speed and test strategy in general; this ticket is the measured
gate with a target.

## Work

- Measure on padme, unloaded, with the load noted: `make check-fast` wall time,
  `pytest --durations=50` under the gate's own selection, and the xdist startup
  cost (`-n 16` against serial on a trivial selection).
- Move each test that reads real data, builds a derived artifact, starts a
  subprocess or sleeps out of `check-fast`: `slow` for real-data tests (repo
  convention: a single `@pytest.mark.slow`), `integration` for subprocess and
  sleep, per `pyproject.toml`. Check with `--collect-only` that each moved test
  is still selected by its WP gate, so nothing leaves every gate.
- Where a fast test pays a fixed setup cost per worker, share it or shrink it.
- Correct the "~40 s" in `AGENTS.md` and [[1060]] to the measured value.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `make check-fast` takes 10 s or less of wall time on padme, measured three
      times unloaded, with the pytest summary line quoted from an unfiltered log
- [ ] Every test moved out of `check-fast` is still selected by a WP gate or by
      `make check` (shown by `--collect-only`)
- [ ] `AGENTS.md` and [[1060]] state the measured duration
